  "summary": "A reciprocating pump in which a smooth solid plunger moves in and out of a pumping chamber through stationary packing. As the plunger withdraws, the chamber pressure falls, the suction valve opens and liquid enters; as it advances, the suction valve closes, pressure rises and the discharge valve opens. Three plungers driven 120° apart (triplex) smooth the flow. Flow depends only on speed and displacement; pressure is limited by rod load and fluid-end strength, so plunger pumps reach very high pressures (water jetting, hydrostatic test, injection).",
  "classification": {
    "family": "Positive displacement – reciprocating",
    "configuration": "Horizontal, triplex, single-acting plunger, crank-driven"
  },
  "model_configuration": {
    "cylinders": 3,
    "stroke_mm": 80.0,
    "crank_phasing": "120°",
    "valves": "Spring-loaded disc (plate) valves",
    "flow_formula": "Q = n_cyl × (π/4·d²) × stroke × N × ηv (single-acting)"
  },
